---
import { url } from '../lib/content';
interface Props { identity: { colours: [string,string][]; headingFont: string; bodyFont: string; direction: string; mark: string }; name: string; slug: string; }
const { identity, name, slug } = Astro.props;
const background = identity.colours[0][1];
const ink = identity.colours[1][1];
const fontCss = "@font-face {\n  font-family: 'Archivo Black';\n  font-style: normal;\n  font-weight: 400;\n  font-display: swap;\n  src: url(__IDENTITY_FONT_ROOT__/archivo-black-0.ttf) format('truetype');\n}\n" + "@font-face {\n  font-family: 'Libre Caslon Display';\n  font-style: normal;\n  font-weight: 400;\n  font-display: swap;\n  src: url(__IDENTITY_FONT_ROOT__/libre-caslon-display-0.ttf) format('truetype');\n}\n@font-face {\n  font-family: 'DM Sans';\n  font-style: normal;\n  font-weight: 400;\n  font-display: swap;\n  src: url(__IDENTITY_FONT_ROOT__/dm-sans-0.ttf) format('truetype');\n}\n@font-face {\n  font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond';\n  font-style: normal;\n  font-weight: 400;\n  font-display: swap;\n  src: url(__IDENTITY_FONT_ROOT__/cormorant-garamond-0.ttf) format('truetype');\n}\n@font-face {\n  font-family: 'Manrope';\n  font-style: normal;\n  font-weight: 400;\n  font-display: swap;\n  src: url(__IDENTITY_FONT_ROOT__/manrope-0.ttf) format('truetype');\n}\n@font-face {\n  font-family: 'Playfair Display';\n  font-style: normal;\n  font-weight: 400;\n  font-display: swap;\n  src: url(__IDENTITY_FONT_ROOT__/playfair-display-0.ttf) format('truetype');\n}\n";

---
<style is:global set:html={fontCss.replaceAll('__IDENTITY_FONT_ROOT__',url('fonts/identity').replace(/\/$/,''))}/><section id="colour-theme"><p class="eyebrow">02 / COLOUR THEME</p><h2>A palette with purpose.</h2><div class="brand-swatches">{identity.colours.map(([label,hex]) => <div><div class="brand-swatch" style={`background:${hex}`} aria-hidden="true"></div><h3>{label}</h3><p>{hex}</p></div>)}</div><p class="identity-note">Colours taken from the website’s styles.</p></section>
<section id="typography"><p class="eyebrow">03 / TYPOGRAPHY</p><h2>Character &amp; clarity.</h2><div class="brand-type"><div><span class="eyebrow">HEADINGS / {identity.headingFont}</span><p class="brand-type-display" style={`font-family: "${identity.headingFont}", Georgia, serif`}>{identity.mark}</p><p class="type-alphabet" style={`font-family: "${identity.headingFont}", Georgia, serif`}>Aa Bb Cc · 0123456789</p></div><div style={`font-family: "${identity.bodyFont}", Arial, sans-serif`}><span class="eyebrow">BODY / {identity.bodyFont}</span><p>Simple, readable supporting text gives the name room to stand out.</p></div></div><p class="identity-note">The website uses {identity.headingFont} with {identity.bodyFont}. </p></section>
<section id="logo-approaches"><p class="eyebrow">04 / LOGO APPROACHES</p><h2>One identity.<br/>Different settings.</h2>{slug === 'sift-and-saffron' ? <div class="brand-logos">{[['sift-primary.svg','Primary wordmark'],['sift-reverse.svg','Reversed wordmark'],['sift-profile.svg','Compact profile mark']].map(([file,label]) => <figure><img src={url('images/portfolio/identity/'+file)} alt={label+' for '+name} width="1000" height="650" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>{label}<a class="text-link" href={url('images/portfolio/identity/'+file)} download>Download SVG ↓</a></figcaption></figure>)}</div> : <div class="brand-logos"><figure><div class="brand-wordmark" style={`background:${background};color:${ink};font-family:"${identity.headingFont}",Georgia,serif`}>{identity.mark}</div><figcaption>Wordmark on a light background</figcaption></figure><figure><div class="brand-wordmark" style={`background:${ink};color:${background};font-family:"${identity.headingFont}",Georgia,serif`}>{identity.mark}</div><figcaption>Reversed wordmark</figcaption></figure></div>}<p class="identity-note">{slug === 'sift-and-saffron' ? 'The wordmark follows the bakery website’s lowercase styling. The reversed version and compact S&S mark are portfolio extensions for dark backgrounds and small profile spaces.' : 'Wordmark studies adapted from the website identity for light and dark backgrounds, shown in the brand’s heading typography.'}</p></section>
